This product includes modified software from the Open Tag Example in the MFS
project, developed by Zilliz (https://github.com/zilliztech/mfs), licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The original example is available at:
https://github.com/zilliztech/mfs/tree/main/examples/open-tag-skill

Tag's modifications include additional chat transports, backend integrations,
operational tooling, scoped MFS helpers, Slack message handling, tests, and
release documentation. The repository history records those changes.

The Codex App Server transport builds on safeguards from OpenTag
(https://github.com/first-tree-ai/opentag), available under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Tag's request lifecycle and Slack event mapping are original to
this project.

Routine scheduling takes its rules and test scenarios from Hermes Agent
(https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent) and OpenClaw
(https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw), both available under the MIT License,
and from Temporal and Kubernetes. The code is original to this project.

Each Tag's knowledge history is written with Dulwich
(https://github.com/jelmer/dulwich), which its authors offer under either the
Apache License, Version 2.0, or the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
later. Tag uses Dulwich under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It is installed
as a dependency, not included in this repository.
